# Component Development Guide

## Next.js React Components

This guide covers development for the [packages/next-react](mdc:packages/next-react) package.

## Project Structure

### Core Directories
- **[components/](mdc:packages/next-react/components)** - Main component library
- **[components/ui/](mdc:packages/next-react/components/ui)** - Reusable UI components
- **[hooks/](mdc:packages/next-react/hooks)** - Custom React hooks
- **[lib/](mdc:packages/next-react/lib)** - Utility functions and configurations
- **[app/](mdc:packages/next-react/app)** - Next.js App Router pages and layouts

### Testing & Documentation
- **[__tests__/](mdc:packages/next-react/__tests__)** - Test files for components and hooks
- **[.storybook/](mdc:packages/next-react/.storybook)** - Storybook configuration
- **[storybook-static/](mdc:packages/next-react/storybook-static)** - Generated Storybook build

## Component Development Standards

### File Organization
```
components/
├── ComponentName.tsx          # Main component
├── ComponentName.stories.tsx  # Storybook stories
└── __tests__/
    └── ComponentName.test.tsx # Component tests
```

### Component Architecture
- Follow patterns from existing components like [LoginForm.tsx](mdc:packages/next-react/components/LoginForm.tsx)
- Use TypeScript interfaces for props
- Implement proper error boundaries and loading states
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions

### Storybook Integration
- Create stories for all UI components
- Document component variants and use cases  
- Include controls for interactive testing
- Use Storybook for visual regression testing

## Configuration Files

### Build & Development
- **[next.config.ts](mdc:packages/next-react/next.config.ts)** - Next.js configuration
- **[components.json](mdc:packages/next-react/components.json)** - Component generation settings
- **[postcss.config.mjs](mdc:packages/next-react/postcss.config.mjs)** - PostCSS configuration

### Testing Setup
- **[vitest.config.ts](mdc:packages/next-react/vitest.config.ts)** - Vitest configuration
- **[vitest-setup.ts](mdc:packages/next-react/vitest-setup.ts)** - Test environment setup
- **[vitest.shims.d.ts](mdc:packages/next-react/vitest.shims.d.ts)** - TypeScript shims

## Development Workflow

### Creating New Components
1. Create component file in appropriate directory
2. Add TypeScript interfaces for props
3. Implement component with proper error handling
4. Create Storybook stories
5. Write comprehensive tests
6. Update documentation

### Testing Components
```bash
# Run component tests
cd packages/next-react
pnpm test

# Run Storybook
pnpm storybook

# Build for production
pnpm build
```

### UI/UX Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow Instagram-inspired design patterns
- Ensure mobile-responsive design
- Implement proper accessibility features
- Use consistent spacing and typography

### Next.js Specific Rules
- Use `'use client'` only at component boundaries that need client-side features
- Leverage App Router for routing and layouts
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized images

## Testing with Playwright

After implementing UI components:
1. Use Playwright to verify visual behavior
2. Generate automated test code
3. Take screenshots for visual regression testing
4. Ensure cross-browser compatibility
